# hashiru.conf — per-machine overrides. Copy to hashiru.conf (gitignored) to use.
#
# Sourced by lib/common.sh before any default is applied, so use the
# `: "${VAR=value}"` form: it sets the variable only when unset, which keeps
# one-off environment overrides working:
#
#   HASHIRU_DOTFILES_REPO= ./install.sh 60
#
# Note `=` and not `:=` — the latter would treat an explicit empty value as
# unset, and empty is meaningful here (it means "no dotfiles").

# Personal dotfiles repo cloned and stowed by 60-dotfiles.sh. Set to the empty
# string to skip dotfiles entirely — Hashiru's own config lives in stow/ and
# does not depend on this.
#: "${HASHIRU_DOTFILES_REPO=https://github.com/you/dotfiles.git}"

# Where that repo is cloned to.
#: "${HASHIRU_DOTFILES_DIR=${HOME}/.dotfiles}"
